This repository contains data tables generated from, and test material copied
from, the third-party works listed below. Each is distributed under its own
license, reproduced or referenced here. Apart from the documentation examples
in section 8 (DataWeave scripts used as test inputs), the generated tables
record data (names, codes, mappings, interface declarations), not program
logic. The generators under
tools/ read the listed artifacts only when the tables are regenerated and are
not needed to build mulay.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Unicode Character Database 16.0.0
   File:    src/mulay/lib/unitab.clay (generated by tools/gen-unicode.py)
   Source:  https://www.unicode.org/Public/16.0.0/ucd/ (general categories,
            case mappings, binary properties, scripts, blocks, property
            value aliases)
   License: Unicode License v3 (full text in section A below)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Locale and time zone display names from OpenJDK 17 (java.time)
   Files:   src/mulay/lib/time/locales.clay (generated by
            tools/gen-locale-data.java)
            src/mulay/lib/time/names.clay (generated by
            tools/gen-time-golden.java)
   Source:  The output of java.time formatting in OpenJDK 17, whose locale
            data comes from the Unicode Common Locale Data Repository (CLDR)
            v39 and, for time zone names that CLDR does not provide, from
            OpenJDK's own time zone name resources.
   License: CLDR: Unicode, Inc. License Agreement - Data Files and Software
            (full text in section B below).
            OpenJDK: GNU General Public License, version 2, with the
            Classpath Exception (https://openjdk.org/legal/gplv2+ce.html).

   Time zone rules (the IANA tz database) are not included in this
   repository; mulay reads them at run time from the host
   (/usr/share/zoneinfo or $TZDIR).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Apache Tika MIME type registry
   File:    src/mulay/conn/sftp_mimes.clay (generated by
            tools/gen-sftp-mimes.java)
   Source:  tika-mimetypes.xml as bundled in mule-sftp-connector 2.7.3
            (Apache Tika, https://tika.apache.org/)
   License: Apache License, Version 2.0
            Apache Tika
            Copyright The Apache Software Foundation
            This product includes software developed at
            The Apache Software Foundation (https://www.apache.org/).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Apache Commons Validator top-level domain list
   File:    src/mulay/lib/tlds.clay (generated by tools/gen-tlds.java)
   Source:  org.apache.commons.validator.routines.DomainValidator in
            commons-validator 1.10.1 (itself derived from the IANA root
            zone database)
   License: Apache License, Version 2.0
            Apache Commons Validator
            Copyright 2002-2025 The Apache Software Foundation
            This product includes software developed at
            The Apache Software Foundation (https://www.apache.org/).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. SQLite result codes and messages
   File:    src/mulay/db/sqlite_codes.clay (generated by
            tools/gen-sqlite-codes.java)
   Source:  org.sqlite.SQLiteErrorCode in xerial sqlite-jdbc 3.50.3.0
            (https://github.com/xerial/sqlite-jdbc); the codes themselves are
            those of SQLite (public domain)
   License: Apache License, Version 2.0

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. Salesforce Metadata API type table
   File:    src/mulay/conn/sf_metatypes.clay (generated by
            tools/gen-sf-metatypes.py)
   Source:  The names and field types of the Metadata API classes in
            force-metadata-api 65.0.0 (Salesforce WSC,
            https://github.com/forcedotcom/wsc), and the type-name mapping of
            mule-salesforce-connector 11.3.4. Only names and types are
            recorded (an interface description); no code is copied.
   License: force-metadata-api: BSD License (FreeBSD), as declared in its
            Maven POM.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. Oracle time zone IDs and SQLState mapping
   Files:   src/mulay/db/ora_zones.clay (generated by tools/gen-ora-zones.java)
            src/mulay/db/ora_sqlstate.clay (generated by
            tools/gen-ora-sqlstate.java)
   Source:  Factual mapping tables read from the Oracle JDBC driver ojdbc11
            23.8.0.25.04 (oracle.sql.ZONEIDMAP: Oracle's numeric time zone
            region IDs to IANA zone names; oracle.jdbc.driver.SQLStateMapping:
            ORA error number ranges to SQLState and exception class). Only
            these number/name correspondences, which are needed to speak the
            Oracle wire protocol, are recorded; no driver code is included.
            The driver itself is distributed by Oracle under the Oracle Free
            Distribution, Hosting, and Use Terms and Conditions.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8. MuleSoft DataWeave documentation examples
   Files:   test/fixtures/dw-docs-corpus/ (extracted by
            tools/extract-dw-corpus.py --docs)
            test/fixtures/dw/docs/ (extracted by tools/docs-fixtures/)
            test/fixtures/dwparse/docs.golden (sources from dw-docs-corpus)
   Source:  The [source,dataweave] examples (scripts, inputs and outputs) of
            the DataWeave 2 documentation, https://github.com/mulesoft/docs-dataweave
            (branch v2.11). Expected outputs were re-computed with DataWeave.
   License: BSD 3-Clause License (full text in section C below)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9. DataWeave 2 standard library declarations
   Files:   src/mulay/dw/stdlib_locs.clay (generated by
            tools/gen-stdlib-locs.py; the NATIVE-TEXT table)
            src/mulay/dw/fnarity.clay (generated by tools/gen-fn-arity.py)
            docs/dw-stdlib-catalog.md
   Source:  The function declarations (names, type signatures, the
            annotations @Since / @Deprecated / @Experimental / @Internal and
            the names of the native bindings) of the .dwl modules in
            wlang-2.11.2.jar and mule-service-weave-2.11.2.jar as shipped with
            Mule 4.11.3. Only these interface declarations are recorded, so
            that mulay accepts the same calls and reports the same error
            locations as DataWeave; no function bodies, documentation text or
            other implementation is copied. DataWeave is a product of
            MuleSoft LLC, a Salesforce company.

